course: dictionary
lesson: 11711
title: Augmented: made bigger or added to
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Augmented is a formal word. It means made bigger or added to. «The shop augmented its stock with new toys before Christmas.» The clue is «with new toys»: the shop added things to what it already had, so its stock grew.
explain: Look for the word that the sentence is about. In «Her pocket money was augmented by a paper round», the paper round gives extra money, so augmented means increased. Everyday speech would say «boosted» or «added to», and those words fit just as well.
explain: Augmented can also be a computer word. Augmented reality is a computer picture added on top of the real world, seen through a phone or glasses. «Sam saw extra labels float above the shelves» is an example: the shop is real, but the labels are added.
fact: Augmented means made bigger or added to.
fact: Augmented is a formal word, used more in writing and exams than in chatting.
fact: Augmented reality (AR) puts computer pictures into the real world you can see through a phone or glasses.
fact: In music, an augmented chord or interval is made a bit wider.
fact: Similar words: increased, boosted, added to.
exercise: «The farmer augmented his hay with extra straw.» What does augmented mean here? | Frozen solid | *Made bigger or added to | Taken away | Painted red
exercise: Ruby's game shows a dragon on her real kitchen table, seen through her phone. What kind of reality is this? | A closed room with no windows | *Augmented reality | Fantasy story | Old reality
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to augmented? | Frozen | Shrunk | Whispered | *Boosted
test: «The chef augmented the soup with fresh herbs.» What does augmented mean in this sentence? | *Made bigger or added to | Cooled down | Thrown away | Hidden under a lid
test: In music, what is an augmented interval? | *An interval made a bit wider | A song sung by a choir | A chord played very softly | An interval made a bit narrower
exam: «Using her glasses, Sam saw extra labels float above the shelves.» What is the best description of augmented reality? | A real world with no pictures at all | A dream you have at night | A film shot in a studio | *A computer picture added on top of the real world you can see
